  "statement": "`n` villages lie on a line at integer positions `p_i`, each with a weight `w_i`. You build one depot at an integer position `x` with `0 ≤ x ≤ L`. Village `i` pays `w_i · |x − p_i|`. Choose `x` to minimise the **largest** payment among all villages and print that minimum value.\n\n**Input.** First line `n L`. Then `n` lines `p_i w_i`.\n\n**Output.** One integer.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n3 10\n0 1\n10 1\n4 2\n```\nOutput:\n```\n5\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 800 in this browser version",
    "1 ≤ L ≤ 10^6, 0 ≤ p_i ≤ L",
    "1 ≤ w_i ≤ 1000"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 1000,
