  "hints": [
    "Plot `f(x) = max_i w_i |x - p_i|`. A maximum of V-shaped functions is itself V-shaped (convex). So it falls and then rises.",
    "On a convex integer sequence, compare `f(mid)` and `f(mid+1)`: if `f(mid) <= f(mid+1)` the minimum is at `mid` or to the left.",
    "Binary search for the first `x` with `f(x) <= f(x + 1)`, then print `f(x)`. Beware the plateau: use `<=`, not `<`."
  ],
  "editorial": "Each `w_i |x - p_i|` is convex, and a maximum of convex functions is convex. A convex function on integers is non-increasing then non-decreasing, so the predicate `f(x) <= f(x+1)` is `F…F T…T`: binary search its first true index in `[0, L]` (`L` itself acts as the sentinel). The minimum value is `f` at that point.\n\nThis is the 'binary search on the discrete derivative' form of ternary search: one evaluation pair per step instead of two thirds, and it behaves correctly on flat tops/bottoms where plain ternary search with strict comparisons can discard the wrong side. Cost `O(n log L)`. Products reach `1000 · 10^6 = 10^9`, so 64-bit is safest.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n\n# Minimise a convex max-of-linear function over integer x.\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// Minimise a convex max-of-linear function over integer x.\n// readLine() returns the next line of input (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    // Minimise a convex max-of-linear function over integer x.\n    // your code here\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        // Minimise a convex max-of-linear function over integer x.\n        // your code here\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    d = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n, L = int(d[0]), int(d[1])\n    ps = [(int(d[2 + 2 * i]), int(d[3 + 2 * i])) for i in range(n)]\n\n    def f(x):\n        return max(w * abs(x - p) for p, w in ps)\n\n    lo, hi = 0, L                    # first x with f(x) <= f(x + 1)\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if f(mid) <= f(mid + 1):\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    print(f(lo))\n\nmain()\n",
    "javascript": "const __L = [];\nlet __s;\nwhile ((__s = readLine()) !== null) __L.push(__s);\nconst T = __L.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter((x) => x.length).map(Number);\nconst n = T[0], L = T[1];\nfunction f(x) {\n  let m = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    m = Math.max(m, T[3 + 2 * i] * Math.abs(x - T[2 + 2 * i]));\n  }\n  return m;\n}\nlet lo = 0, hi = L;\nwhile (lo < hi) {\n  const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);\n  if (f(mid) <= f(mid + 1)) hi = mid; else lo = mid + 1;\n}\nconsole.log(String(f(lo)));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static StreamTokenizer st;\n\n    static long nl() throws IOException {\n        st.nextToken();\n        return (long) st.nval;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        st = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        int n = (int) nl();\n        int L = (int) nl();\n        long[] p = new long[n], w = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            p[i] = nl();\n            w[i] = nl();\n        }\n        int lo = 0, hi = L;\n        while (lo < hi) {\n            int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            if (f(mid, p, w) <= f(mid + 1, p, w)) hi = mid; else lo = mid + 1;\n        }\n        System.out.println(f(lo, p, w));\n        }\n\n        static long f(long x, long[] p, long[] w) {\n            long m = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < p.length; i++) m = Math.max(m, w[i] * Math.abs(x - p[i]));\n            return m;\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nlong long f(long long x, const vector<long long> &p, const vector<long long> &w) {\n    long long m = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < p.size(); i++) m = max(m, w[i] * llabs(x - p[i]));\n    return m;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    long long L;\n    scanf(\"%d %lld\", &n, &L);\n    vector<long long> p(n), w(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%lld %lld\", &p[i], &w[i]);\n    long long lo = 0, hi = L;\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        long long mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n        if (f(mid, p, w) <= f(mid + 1, p, w)) hi = mid; else lo = mid + 1;\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", f(lo, p, w));\n}\n"
  }
